Hi Redstage team,

We sent you a client security audit for citgo.com with a published grade of D=
 (45/100). That grade was wrong. Our scoring model at the time penalised ever=
y finding flatly and counted best-practice configuration items as vulnerabili=
ties. Re-scoring the same scan under the corrected model gives C (60/100).

Three finding classes drove the wrong grade: the SSL/TLS certificate verifica=
tion failure, the SSL/TLS connection failure and the missing DNS and disclosu=
re records (CAA, security.txt).

Two critical or high findings in that report are unaffected by this correctio=
n and still need attention.

The rule now: best-practice items are reported but never scored, a scan with =
no critical or high finding cannot score below 60, and repeated findings of t=
he same class are charged at a reduced rate under a per-class cap.

Next step: reply to this note and we will re-issue the citgo.com audit with t=
he corrected grade and score. No change to the client's configuration is requ=
ired to correct the score.

